     <p>The mean hydrophobicity &lt;H&gt; is read over the whole quinolone resistance-determining region helix of each enzyme: GyrA 82-93 (D<b>S</b>AVY<b>D</b>TIVRMA, 12 residues) and ParC 80-90 (<b>S</b>ACY<b>E</b>AMVLMA, 11 residues). The four tetratype positions (in bold) take the sample&#39;s residues and the others stay fixed. The GyrA helix mean is the sum of H over 12, the ParC helix mean is the sum over 11, and &lt;H&gt; = (GyrA mean + ParC mean) / 2. The three values are also in the JSON download and the API for every isolate.</p>
